%I A365191 #24 Aug 04 2026 17:12:04
%S A365191 24,94,259,593
%N A365191 The weak Schur numbers for 3-coloring.
%C A365191 a(6) >= 1146 and a(7) >= 2005 (see Ahmed et al., Table 6).
%C A365191 From _Alper Ferudun_, Jul 28 2026: (Start)
%C A365191 a(k) = WS_k(3), the least N such that every 3-coloring of [1,N] has distinct same-colored x_1,...,x_k whose sum has the same color.
%C A365191 a(5) = 593: the coloring of [1,592] in Ahmed et al. gives the lower bound, and an exhaustive SAT computation modulo permutations of the three colors gives the upper bound. (End)
%H A365191 T. Ahmed, L. Boza, M. P. Revuelta, and M. I. Sanz, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1007/s11139-023-00760-y">Exact values and lower bounds on the n-color weak Schur numbers for n=2,3</a>. Ramanujan J (2023). See Table 6 at p. 8 and Sections 4.3 and 4.4 at pp. 13-16.
%H A365191 Alper Ferudun, <a href="/A365191/a365191_1.cpp.txt">Self-contained C++20 program for a(5)</a>
%o A365191 (C++) // See Links.
%Y A365191 Cf. A030126, A045652, A072842, A118771, A365190 (similar for 2-coloring).
%K A365191 nonn,hard,more
%O A365191 2,1
%A A365191 _Stefano Spezia_, Aug 25 2023
%E A365191 a(5) added by _Alper Ferudun_, Jul 28 2026
